        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "A mixture of H2picO (0.028 g, 0.2 mmol), DyCl3·6H2O (0.038 g, 0.1 mmol), Phen (0.018 g, 0.1 mmol), aqueous NaOH (0.4 mL, 0.65 mol L−1) and deionized water (3 mL) was sealed in a 25 mL Teflon-lined stainless vessel and heated at 140 °C for 12 h under autogenous pressure. Colorless cubic crystals formed on cooling to room temperature, were filtered, washed with deionized water and ethanol, and dried in air. The main text only states that the synthesis followed the Er(III)/Yb(III) analogues but at 140 °C for 12 h.",
