        "summary": "Linear Dy3 single-molecule magnet. χT falls from 43.03 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K to 19.11 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K under 1000 Oe, and magnetization reaches 15.46 μB at 2 K and 7 T, consistent with magnetic anisotropy. Under zero dc field, slow relaxation is dominated by Raman and QTM processes. Under 2000 Oe, slow and fast Orbach processes have barriers of 30 ± 1 K and 39 ± 32 K, respectively.",
